cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: iEEG Prep
abstract: The first step of the epilepsy iEEG workflows. Reads BIDS-iEEG datasets (MNE-BIDS) or plain
  EDF, BrainVision, FIF and MEF3 recordings with optional expert labels, keeps the SEEG/ECoG channels,
  finds bad channels, re-references (bipolar by default), notch- and high-pass-filters, and writes one
  BIDS-iEEG derivative (EDF+ with per-channel range and sidecars carrying SOZ, resected, onset and
  spread labels and coordinates) plus a QC table and figures.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/processor-ieeg-prep
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- ieeg
- seeg
- ecog
- epilepsy
- electrophysiology
- bids
- preprocessing
- quality-control
